    "body": "## Summary\n`main` is red on `cpu_unit_tests`: after #8010 (score centering) and #7945 (Liger TP fused CE) both landed, the megatron liger CPU test builds a lightweight config via a monkeypatched `omega_conf_to_dataclass` that returns a `SimpleNamespace` without `policy_loss`, while `ActorRolloutRefWorker.init_model` reads `actor_config.policy_loss...` unconditionally → `AttributeError`.\n\n- Reproduces on `main` itself: latest main run (4b26c788) job `117718352932`, `1 failed, 1503 passed` —\n  `FAILED tests/workers/test_megatron_liger_fused_kernels_on_cpu.py::test_worker_reserves_both_consumers_before_ref_reset - AttributeError: 'types.SimpleNamespace' object has no attribute 'policy_loss'`.\n- Guard the lookup with `getattr(..., None)`; absent `policy_loss` selects the default `ppo_loss`, identical to an empty-default `PolicyLossConfig`.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Verified the guarded conditional returns the same result as the original expression for: missing attribute, empty `policy_loss`, `rollout_correction` present without centering, and centering enabled.\n- [ ] `cpu_unit_tests` green on this PR.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
